        "original_id": "1993017d-b5f4-54c3-8536-afabc48d22a7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 1946 National League tie-breaker series, 1946 World Series\n- Teams: Brooklyn Dodgers, St. Louis Cardinals\n- People: Clyde Kluttz\n- Seasons: 1946 Brooklyn Dodgers season\n\nFacts:\n- In 1946, the Brooklyn Dodgers finished the regular season tied for first place with the St. Louis Cardinals.\n- In 1946, the Brooklyn Dodgers and the St. Louis Cardinals both finished the season with identical 96–58 records.\n- In 1946, the National League tie-breaker series was necessary because the Brooklyn Dodgers and the St. Louis Cardinals finished with identical 96–58 records.\n- In 1946, Clyde Kluttz appeared in 52 regular season games for the world champion St. Louis Cardinals.\n- On October 3, 1946, Clyde Kluttz was the starting catcher for the St. Louis Cardinals in the flag-clinching Game 2 of the postseason playoff against the Brooklyn Dodgers.\n- In 1946, Clyde Kluttz did not play in the World Series.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
